  "caption": "Hot day, 30-minute walk, six water bottles. Quinn drank them all on schedule and ended up bloated and queasy.\n\nFor most people, thirst is a good guide, and over-drinking is the riskier mistake. Sweat rates vary a lot between people, and bodies adapt to the heat with time.\n\nWhat often helps: starting well hydrated and drinking when thirsty, choosing cool drinks, adding electrolytes or a sports drink for long, hot sessions beyond about an hour or if you sweat salty, salting food normally, and easing into hot-weather training.\n\nHeadache, nausea, bloating or weight gain during a long event can point to over-drinking, so get checked. Confusion, repeated vomiting, collapse or very hot skin is an emergency: call 000.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
